<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gherardo Appiani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1405">1405</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gherardo Appiani was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a> who in 1399 sold the city to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> while keeping Piombino, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elba">Elba</a> and nearby islands for himself. This created the lordship, later principality, of Piombino, which his family ruled until the early 17th century.</p></div>
